  "rules": [
    "<strong>Review 3x/week:</strong> Monday close, Wednesday close, Friday close. Friday = Baker Hughes rig data.",
    "<strong>Never deploy > 1/3 SGOV</strong> on one signal. Budget: $1,200/month.",
    "<strong>No single stock > 10%</strong> of total book. No overlay > 2.5% except OIH at 5%.",
    "<strong>No naked calls.</strong> 90-120 DTE spreads only. 2% premium cap.",
    "<strong>De-escalation protocol:</strong> Brent < $95 for 5 closes + restored traffic → cut XOP 1/3, CF/NTR 1/4, close tankers, rebuild VXUS + SGOV.",
    "<strong>Don't force services.</strong> Rigs falling = no OIH/HAL/SLB, even if oil is high.",
    "<strong>Graph propagation:</strong> When upstream node fires, check all downstream edges. Estimated lags are planning windows, not execution triggers.",
    "<strong>Confluence rule:</strong> Nodes with 3+ incoming fired edges get highest conviction. em-stress is the primary confluence node.",
    "<strong>Analog calibration:</strong> Use 2008 template lags as planning baseline. Current crisis is 4 weeks in — employment impact expected by late June 2026.",
    "<strong>Scenario discipline:</strong> Trade the probability-weighted portfolio, not any single scenario. Reopen-apr1 (10%) means maintain positions."
  ],
